{"engine":"Windows.Media.Ocr en-US","scale":3,"pages":[{"page":1,"width":2436,"height":3156,"lines":[{"text":"This isn't the first time we've heard from this lone opponent of funding our schools. He doesn't live","x":322,"y":329,"w":1777,"h":47},{"text":"in the County, let alone our community. If he did, he'd know Burlingame's rich history of supporting","x":323,"y":381,"w":1796,"h":47},{"text":"local schools, making our community strong and such a special place to call home.","x":322,"y":434,"w":1455,"h":46},{"text":"We feel obligated to set thc record straight and remind our neighbors why we need Measure R:","x":322,"y":538,"w":1675,"h":47},{"text":"Some of Our Schools Are Over 100 Years Old. And their age is showing. Classrooms","x":460,"y":644,"w":1556,"h":45},{"text":"suffer from dry rot, leaky roofs, and outdated plumbing and electrical systems. Students are","x":460,"y":694,"w":1614,"h":48},{"text":"learning in outdated classrooms.","x":458,"y":749,"w":570,"h":45},{"text":"Basic Repairs and Upgrades. Measure R removes hazardous materials like lead and","x":459,"y":798,"w":1519,"h":48},{"text":"asbestos, replaces aging pipes and roofing, and updates science, technology, engineering, and","x":457,"y":849,"w":1640,"h":49},{"text":"math labs, giving teachers the tools to prepare students for high school, college, and beyond.","x":457,"y":901,"w":1638,"h":48},{"text":"100% of Funds Stay Local. By law, funds can only be used in Burlingame schools. No","x":458,"y":954,"w":1551,"h":45},{"text":"funds can be taken by the State or Federal Government.","x":458,"y":1007,"w":993,"h":45},{"text":"A Clear System of Accountability. An independent citizens' oversight committee and","x":453,"y":1055,"w":1555,"h":49},{"text":"mandatory annual independent audits are required to make sure every penny is spent as","x":456,"y":1109,"w":1548,"h":47},{"text":"voters intend.","x":456,"y":1163,"w":240,"h":33},{"text":"Measure R keeps our tradition of academic excellence, protecting what makes Burlingame such a","x":320,"y":1264,"w":1716,"h":49},{"text":"special place to live: strong schools, strong community, and strong students.","x":320,"y":1317,"w":1336,"h":48},{"text":"Let's make the essential, basic repairs and upgrades our schools need. Join teachers, small","x":318,"y":1421,"w":1750,"h":48},{"text":"businesses, and community leaders — Vote Yes on Measure R!","x":318,"y":1476,"w":1214,"h":44},{"text":"RECEIVED","x":726,"y":1768,"w":302,"h":62},{"text":"AUG 1 8","x":755,"y":1868,"w":157,"h":52}]},{"page":2,"width":2436,"height":3156,"lines":[{"text":"OFFICE OF","x":638,"y":226,"w":244,"h":37},{"text":"ASSESSOR-COUNTY CLERK-","x":635,"y":288,"w":674,"h":48},{"text":"RECORDER & ELECTIONS","x":638,"y":362,"w":594,"h":47},{"text":"COUNTY OF SAN MATEO","x":637,"y":438,"w":548,"h":38},{"text":"MARK CHURCH","x":1693,"y":275,"w":373,"h":44},{"text":"CHIEF ELECTIONS OFFICER &","x":1630,"y":335,"w":498,"h":36},{"text":"ASSESSOR-COUNTY CLERK-RECORDER","x":1555,"y":382,"w":651,"h":35},{"text":"Authorization Form for","x":960,"y":606,"w":583,"h":41},{"text":"Change in Signers of Rebuttal Arguments","x":720,"y":667,"w":1059,"h":53},{"text":"Pursuant to California Elections Code SS9167, 9317 and 9504, the author(s) of the primary","x":253,"y":777,"w":1838,"h":49},{"text":"argument in favor of or against a measure may authorize in writing any other person or persons to","x":251,"y":858,"w":1986,"h":47},{"text":"sign the rebuttal argument.","x":250,"y":939,"w":543,"h":45},{"text":"The undersigned author(s) of the primary argument hereby authorize(s) the following","x":250,"y":1094,"w":1853,"h":49},{"text":"individual(s) to sign (up to five) the rebuttal argument to the primary argument in favor","x":251,"y":1174,"w":1885,"h":49},{"text":"one) Measure","x":626,"y":1256,"w":296,"h":46},{"text":"NEW SIGNER(S) (PRINT CLEARLY):","x":250,"y":1405,"w":778,"h":45},{"text":"Name of Rebuttal Argument Signer:","x":250,"y":1534,"w":722,"h":45},{"text":"Name of Rebuttal 